{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which Qualifi Level 3 Diplomas are available?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Eight Level 3 Diplomas are offered across business, management, entrepreneurship, health and social care, hospitality and tourism, accounting and finance, and information technology — giving you a foundation-level entry point into whichever career direction you choose."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Qualifi a recognised awarding organisation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Qualifi is an Ofqual-recognised awarding organisation. Its regulated qualifications have individual records and qualification numbers, so check the exact diploma title and current regulatory status rather than relying on the organisation's name alone. Regulation establishes qualification standards; it does not guarantee acceptance by every employer, professional body or receiving university."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is a Level 3 Diploma, and who is it for?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A Level 3 Diploma is a foundation-level qualification — the stage that prepares you for higher-level study or your first professional roles. It suits school-leavers, career starters and career changers who want a structured, recognised entry point into a field without committing to a full degree straight away."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What do I need to enrol in a Level 3 Diploma?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Level 3 entry requirements depend on the subject and qualification specification. The centre assesses whether your educational background and English-language ability prepare you for the course, along with any minimum age or other conditions. Ask for the current entry checklist rather than assuming that every foundation-level diploma has open entry."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does a Level 3 Diploma cost to study?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Ask for the full cost of the Level 3 diploma you choose. The quotation should state the currency, tuition and any registration, assessment or certification charges. If a payment plan or fee reduction is offered, check its conditions and total cost. Entry-level study does not mean that all subjects have the same fee or funding arrangements."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can I progress to after a Level 3 Diploma?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A Level 3 diploma may support entry-level work or progression to higher study in a related field. The next qualification depends on subject fit and its entry criteria; Level 4 study may form part of an Extended Level 5 route. Ask for an agreed pathway rather than assuming that every Level 3 award gives automatic admission to Level 5."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which Level 5 Extended Diplomas can I choose from?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The supplied portfolio lists fourteen Level 5 Extended Diplomas, covering business, health and social care, psychology, hospitality and tourism, accounting, law, information technology and its specialist tracks, cyber security, occupational health and safety, and education and training management. Match your intended subject to the current qualification title and specification before applying."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does \"Extended Diploma\" mean at Level 5?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "An Extended Diploma combines a larger body of study than a standard diploma at the same level, commonly bringing together Level 4 and Level 5 learning. Published Qualifi specifications include 240-credit routes. Check the exact diploma's credit structure; study volume alone does not establish automatic equivalence to two university years or guarantee credit transfer."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which level should I start at — Level 3 or Level 5?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Choose the level that matches your existing qualifications and subject preparation. Level 3 can provide a foundation for further study, while an Extended Level 5 route normally includes higher-level learning across Levels 4 and 5. Ask admissions to assess your background against the chosen qualification's criteria; experience does not replace formal prerequisites unless that route permits it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the entry requirements for a Level 5 Extended Diploma?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Entry is assessed against the chosen diploma's published requirements. These may include prior Level 3 or Level 4 qualifications, relevant experience, subject preparation and English-language evidence. An Extended route may contain both levels of study, so confirm where you enter and what you must complete; technical subjects can have different prerequisites from business routes."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the fee structure for a Level 5 Extended Diploma?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Request a quotation covering the entire Extended Diploma route, not just one stage. Check which units or levels are included, the currency, registration and assessment fees, and any available instalment schedule. The credit structure and commercial terms should both be confirmed before you compare this route with a diploma or degree elsewhere."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can a Level 5 Extended Diploma lead to a bachelor's degree?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A Level 5 Extended Diploma may support entry to a bachelor's top-up, and Qualifi publishes degree-progression opportunities for several routes. The receiving university must accept the exact subject, credits and learning outcomes. Confirm the named degree, entry stage and remaining study in writing; holding 240 credits does not automatically guarantee final-year admission everywhere."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which specialisations do the Qualifi Level 7 Diplomas cover?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The supplied portfolio includes twenty-three Level 7 diploma subjects across strategy, leadership, projects, risk, marketing, human resources, finance, law, psychology, health and safety, hospitality, technology, data science, cyber security, supply chain and education management. Compare the exact qualification specifications and entry criteria; sharing a level does not make the subjects or progression routes interchangeable."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Who are the Qualifi Level 7 Diplomas designed for?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "They are built for graduates and experienced professionals who want postgraduate-level certification focused on applied, workplace-ready capability — managers formalising their experience, specialists stepping up to strategic roles, and professionals preparing a bridge towards a full master's qualification."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need a degree to enrol in a Qualifi Level 7 Diploma?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A degree is not the only possible entry route for every diploma, but alternatives must be permitted by the specific qualification. Some routes consider relevant professional experience or other prior study; others require particular academic or subject preparation. Ask admissions to assess the exact diploma criteria rather than assuming a portfolio-wide experience exemption."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long do the Level 7 Diplomas take, and how are they assessed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Study duration and assessment depend on the diploma and approved delivery plan. Ask for the expected timetable, guided and independent study hours, assessment methods and submission deadlines. Assignment-based study may be available, but it should not be assumed that every Level 7 track is self-paced, examination-free or completed within a single short timetable."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How are Level 7 Diploma fees structured?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Level 7 fees can differ by subject, route and intake. Ask for the tuition total, billing currency and any awarding, assessment or additional study charges. If instalments or fee support are offered, compare the total payable and conditions. Programmes at the same qualification level need not have identical prices or payment arrangements."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can I progress to after a Qualifi Level 7 Diploma?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A Level 7 diploma may support further professional development or a master's application, depending on the subject and receiving institution. Management and law diplomas can have different progression arrangements, and the remaining study is not always limited to a dissertation. Confirm the exact receiving award and accepted credits before planning an MBA, LLM or other master's top-up."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What career impact can a Qualifi Level 7 Diploma have?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A Qualifi Level 7 diploma can develop advanced subject knowledge and applied skills relevant to your professional field. It may strengthen evidence for a development or promotion discussion, but employers also assess experience and performance. A diploma does not automatically confer seniority, professional registration or a guaranteed career outcome."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I stack Qualifi diplomas over time — Level 3, then 5, then 7?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You can plan further qualifications over time, but progression is not automatic. Each completed diploma is an award in its own right. Entry to the next level depends on its subject and requirements; additional Level 4, degree-level study or experience may be needed. Map the complete route before enrolling rather than assuming a direct Level 3-to-5-to-7 ladder."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do Qualifi diplomas expire or need renewing?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "An academic diploma normally remains a record of completed study, rather than a membership that requires annual renewal. A qualification being withdrawn from new registrations does not, by itself, erase an achieved award. Receiving institutions or professional bodies may nevertheless require recent knowledge or continuing development; check any such rules for your intended use."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Will my certificate show the official accreditation number?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Regulated Qualifi diplomas have an official qualification number that identifies the award in the qualifications register. Ask how it appears on your certificate or supporting documents. The number identifies the qualification, not whether an individual certificate is genuine; employers or institutions should use the awarding body's authorised verification process when checking a personal award."
      }
    }
  ]
}
